WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.670
A customer's phone number vanished somewhere between Salesforce and
the CRM.

2
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.920
Start with the account's Salesforce ID.

3
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.680
Two journeys come back for this account. One completed, and one
failed.

4
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.530
The timeline begins with the webhook and follows work from the
integration service into the worker.

5
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.130
But delivery isn't where it broke. Open the transform step.

6
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.770
This is the payload before and after the step, field by field.

7
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.150
The phone goes in with a value, and comes out null. This is the step
that lost it.

8
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.420
Now the journey that completed, for contrast.

9
00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.470
Its payload carried the field the transform reads, so the phone kept
its value.

10
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:05.170
Back on the failed journey, replay the step's recorded input.

11
00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:11.410
It goes to a development destination running the fix, not to the
original system.

12
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.950
The fixed transform answers with a 200.

13
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.300
Original against replay. The phone was null, and now it's back.

14
00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.720
Wayscribe. Self-hosted, open source, at wayscribe.dev.

